`/pps/pallet_pose_rich` now carries the stage-2 inlier-face extents from the same estimate that produced the pose.

`PalletPoseStamped` has `has_dimensions`, `width_m`, `height_m`, and `depth_m`. Width is the camera-x span, height is the camera-y span, and depth is the mean range, in metres. `publish_pose` copies those values from that estimate only when the estimate produced an inlier face. Otherwise `has_dimensions` is false and the three extents are zero.

